{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses went up.</b> On the second day of the month, which is the third day of the week. And he did not go up on his own, but rather because <b>YHWH called to him from the mountain, saying: Thus you shall say</b> — to teach you that he went up only with permission. And one may say: he went up on his own to ask from the mouth of HaShem how they should serve Him, to fulfill what He said to him, 'When you bring the people out of Egypt, you shall serve Elohim on this mountain.' And HaShem said to him, <b>Thus you shall say to the house of Jacob</b> — if you will surely obey, etc., this shall be My service. Even so, we find at the giving of the Torah: 'they offered burnt offerings and sacrificed sacrifices,' etc." "<b>And you shall tell the children of Israel.</b> Rashi explained: to the males — things as hard as sinews. And in order to expound it thus, it is plene; but according to its plain sense, 'and you shall tell the children of Israel' refers back to 'you have seen what I did,' etc. For the form הגדה never denotes a future matter, but only past."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:41.430287580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}